%% Phase 3: Refinement and review (autonomous, no Owner)
%%
%% The Designer takes its second job here: slicing an approved TEP into Tasks.
%%
%% Waves: Tasks form a dependency graph (depends_on). A topological layer holds tasks that do
%% not depend on each other. The Designer orders layers risk first (the riskiest or most
%% foundational assumption lands in wave 1) and groups consecutive layers into review waves,
%% recording the reason on the Epic. The Owner reviews at wave boundaries (see implementation).
%%
%% Rolling wave: only the next wave is written in full. The rest stay as outlines and are
%% detailed when their dependencies are in the epic branch, so they see the code that landed.
%%
%% Task states in this phase:
%%   outline                                   (title, intent, wave, depends_on; no steps yet)
%%   draft -> in-review -> ready               (approved, waits for dependencies and a worker)
%%                      -> changes-requested -> in-review   (loop, capped)
%%                      -> blocked
%% Constraint on every Task: one PR worth of change, a few commits, a small diff, the build stays
%% green after it.
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber

  box Agents
    participant Des as Designer
    participant Rev as Reviewer
  end

  box Artifacts
    participant TEPs@{ "type" : "collections" }
    participant Epics@{ "type" : "collections" }
    participant Tasks@{ "type" : "collections" }
    participant Backlog@{ "type" : "collections" }
    participant Questions@{ "type" : "collections" }
  end

  Des->>TEPs: pick up a TEP in state approved that has no Tasks yet
  TEPs->>Des: the TEP
  Des->>Des: reads TEP, Epic, ADRs, spec, code
  Des->>Des: slices the TEP into Tasks, builds the depends_on graph
  Des->>Des: orders layers risk first, groups them into review waves
  Des->>Epics: write the wave plan (which Tasks, in which wave, and why)
  Des->>Tasks: write the Tasks of wave 1 in state draft (steps, file list, tests, depends_on)
  Des->>Tasks: write the Tasks of later waves in state outline

  Note over Des,Tasks: Later waves, once their dependencies are in the epic branch
  Des->>Tasks: pick up an outline Task whose dependencies are merged into the epic branch
  Des->>Des: reads the current epic branch, fills in the steps
  Des->>Tasks: Task becomes draft

  Rev->>Tasks: pick up Tasks in state draft
  Tasks->>Rev: the Tasks, the wave plan and the TEP
  Rev->>Rev: fresh context, reads Tasks, TEP, ADRs, spec, code
  Note over Rev: Senior Developer lens: could an implementer build this without deciding anything architectural?<br/>Architect lens: size, independence, conflicts between Tasks, accuracy of depends_on, wave grouping

  alt Blocker or Major findings
    Rev->>Tasks: write findings on the Task. State becomes changes-requested
    Des->>Tasks: pick up a Task in state changes-requested
    Des->>Tasks: fix, or contest with evidence. State becomes in-review
  else Task too large, or the TEP is wrong
    Rev->>Tasks: state becomes blocked
    Rev->>Questions: ask the Owner, or send the TEP back (state amend)
  else only Nits, or no findings
    Rev->>Tasks: state becomes ready
    Rev->>Backlog: nits and ADR candidates become backlog items in state open
  end

  Note over Des,Tasks: Fast path for a bugfix Task written in exploration
  Des->>Tasks: pick up a bugfix Task in state draft (no Epic, no TEP)
  Des->>Tasks: add steps and file list. Same review loop as above
